                        ],
                        "form": "бура́вчике"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4ea501ab-455c-4bf2-aaaa-a2745064622f",
                        "entry_id": "26df3bd3-c69c-3f79-bbfa-6700ca311b4b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "бура́вчиках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9a6ece48-a7b1-3dc2-8faa-158afaad99dc",
                        "entry_id": "26df3bd3-c69c-3f79-bbfa-6700ca311b4b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "уменьш. к бурав; небольшой ручной инструмент для сверления отверстий цилиндрической формы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7942772-d561-4d30-aefa-f17cdf58390d",
                                "sense_id": "9a6ece48-a7b1-3dc2-8faa-158afaad99dc",
                                "text": "Выпросил себе на время у священника, за подрезку винограда, топор, долото, стамеску, молоток и буравчик, обязавшись за них еще прищепить ему несколько дичков яблонь и слив в церковном садике."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a80007e8-7fac-46a4-a3ae-2331a15d1dd1",
                                "sense_id": "9a6ece48-a7b1-3dc2-8faa-158afaad99dc",
                                "text": "В тот же день пришёл техник из домоуправления, с ним какой-то посторонний, по наружности и походке из села или района, сорвали бумагу с гербовой печатью, отперли двери, техник недолго покрутился, человек остался один, вынул из кармана молоток, буравчик, прибил снаружи два кольца, набросил замок и, перед тем как уйти, три раза крепко подергал."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a21fbd3c-5bb1-4cbd-b38c-3c24522f7a2a",
                        "source_entry_id": "26df3bd3-c69c-3f79-bbfa-6700ca311b4b",
                        "source_sense_id": "9a6ece48-a7b1-3dc2-8faa-158afaad99dc",
                        "target_lang_word": "gimlet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gimlet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80c1a6d9-5087-3941-bd82-16a39fc82091",
                                        "entry_id": "6c6365d7-5d49-3c62-912e-5679c676d329",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small screw-tipped tool for boring holes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eee9fdfb-fdf3-48d0-bbd1-cf77d736cdd4",
                                                "sense_id": "80c1a6d9-5087-3941-bd82-16a39fc82091",
                                                "text": "The box was close on every side, with a little door for me to go in and out, and a few gimlet holes to let in air."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7642f41f-938f-43f2-ada3-cbb98d6381a2",
                                                "sense_id": "80c1a6d9-5087-3941-bd82-16a39fc82091",
                                                "text": "I would find by the edge of that water / The collar-bone of a hare / Worn thin by the lapping of water, / And pierce it through with a gimlet and stare [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa513b25-29df-37ba-9f38-55f4c733b128",
                                        "entry_id": "6c6365d7-5d49-3c62-912e-5679c676d329",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cocktail, usually made with gin and lime juice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42454364-8520-415f-b5fc-79f767734fa3",
                                                "sense_id": "aa513b25-29df-37ba-9f38-55f4c733b128",
                                                "text": "We sat in a corner of the bar at Victor's and drank gimlets. “They don't know how to make them here,” he said. “What they call a gimlet is just some lime or lemon juice and gin with a dash of sugar and bitters. A real gimlet is half gin and half Rose's Lime Juice and nothing else. It beats martinis hollow.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbb62374-65d3-484d-9f37-42a8f34eb35d",
                                                "sense_id": "aa513b25-29df-37ba-9f38-55f4c733b128",
                                                "text": "Yeah, a piece of advice — once you’re back in circulation, don’t keep topping off a lady’s vodka gimlet when she’s not looking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a462c2b-60a4-425b-938e-5c532e28e84d",
                                                "sense_id": "aa513b25-29df-37ba-9f38-55f4c733b128",
                                                "text": "By seven, dinner was under way, and a bottle of vodka gimlets and one of martinis were in the freezer, chilling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gimlet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "070e930f-8a11-3951-a9b0-2d29845af36d",
                                        "entry_id": "1ba96864-a279-3104-8ecb-af93b031e9b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pierce or bore holes (as if using a gimlet)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7864208d-f589-4aad-9ea0-db1b34ac9984",
                                                "sense_id": "070e930f-8a11-3951-a9b0-2d29845af36d",
                                                "text": "Then there was an awful silence. The lady gimleted us again one by one with her blue eyes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "670c21cc-b5c7-3057-8254-6acfb25b5cdb",
                                        "entry_id": "1ba96864-a279-3104-8ecb-af93b031e9b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To turn round (an anchor) as if turning a gimlet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
